  clock: 6  # da1f
  nonce: da1f  # da1f
  message: "Pass-33 face: 2 of 5 INV-rakot fields now echoed; 3 still missing (F33.1).\n\nINV-rakot scope (2026-05-28 baseline): slice JSON's `feature.query` field omits `min_confidence, max_tier, hub_threshold, exclude_imports, language`. Pass-33 re-tested against `/tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json` and finds **partial mitigation**:\n\n**Test invocation.**\n```\n$ hypergumbo slice --entry _ws_handler --input bm.json --out X \\\n    --min-confidence 0.5 --max-tier 3 --exclude-tests --hub-threshold 10\n```\n\n**Resulting `feature.query` keys.**\n```\n['entrypoint', 'exclude_tests', 'exclude_utility', 'hops', 'hub_threshold',\n 'max_files', 'max_tier', 'method', 'pass_through_kinds', 'reverse']\n```\n\n**Status against the 5-field gap:**\n- `max_tier` — **NOW PRESENT** (value 3, echoed correctly)\n- `hub_threshold` — **NOW PRESENT** (value 10, echoed correctly)\n- `min_confidence` — **STILL MISSING** (set flag value 0.5 not echoed; query has no min_confidence key)\n- `exclude_imports` — **STILL MISSING** (not tested with flag set, but query has no key)\n- `language` — **STILL MISSING** (no key)\n\nSo 2 of the 5 originally-cataloged missing fields are now populated (40% gap-closure); 3 remain unechoed. The flags themselves accept the values (slice returns exit 0) but `--min-confidence` is silently swallowed — pass-31 F31.4 / INV-fabov family at the slice subcommand layer.\n\n**Status recommendation.** INV-rakot scope reads \"omits min_confidence, max_tier, hub_threshold, exclude_imports, language\" — the title is now factually outdated for 2 of those 5. Three live faces remain. Either:\n1. Update the statement to reflect the current 3-field gap (min_confidence, exclude_imports, language) and keep status `violated`\n2. Flip status to `pending_validation` with the title noting \"partial fix\"\n3. Keep as-is — half-closure isn't closure\n\nPass-33's recommendation: option 1 — update statement to the current 3-field set, mark `partial_mitigation`-tagged, keep status `violated` until all 5 echo. The flags-silently-accepted behavior (especially `--min-confidence`) is the more critical user-facing gap.\n\n**No status change in this pass.** Probe artifact: `/tmp/p33_outputA3.log` section \"A.15\"."  # da1f
- op: discuss  # 67c7
